  ('english-043', 'english', 'choice', 'Machu Picchu', 'These features allowed people ____ comfortably.', '빈칸에 알맞은 것은?', 'For hundreds of years, Machu Picchu remained hidden in the Andes Mountains of Peru. In 1911, an American explorer named Hiram Bingham introduced the ancient city to the world after local people guided him there. Today, millions of visitors travel to see its beautiful stone buildings and breathtaking mountain views. Although many facts about Machu Picchu are known, historians still debate why the city was built and why it was later abandoned. Most experts believe that Machu Picchu was built in the 1400s during the rule of the Inca emperor Pachacuti. The city was probably home to nobles, priests, and skilled workers rather than a large population. People grew crops on stone terraces that covered the mountainside. They also collected fresh water through a system of carefully planned canals and fountains. These features allowed people to live comfortably in a place that was difficult to reach. One of the most impressive features of Machu Picchu is its stonework. The Inca builders shaped huge stones so carefully that they fit together without mortar. This method made the buildings strong enough to survive many earthquakes. Even after hundreds of years of wind, rain, and earthquakes, much of the city still stands. Machu Picchu shows that the Inca people were not only skilled builders but also talented engineers who understood both nature and architecture.

[문제의 대상 문장·표현]
These features allowed people ____ comfortably.', 'to live', array['live', 'living', 'lived'], '{}'::text[], 'allow + 목적어 + to V는 "~가 …하게 해 주다"다. 목적격 보어 자리에 to부정사가 온다.', '학습지1', 3, null, null, 42, null, null),
  ('english-044', 'english', 'choice', 'Machu Picchu', 'Canals allowed people to live there.', 'allow O to V의 뜻으로 알맞은 것은?', 'For hundreds of years, Machu Picchu remained hidden in the Andes Mountains of Peru. In 1911, an American explorer named Hiram Bingham introduced the ancient city to the world after local people guided him there. Today, millions of visitors travel to see its beautiful stone buildings and breathtaking mountain views. Although many facts about Machu Picchu are known, historians still debate why the city was built and why it was later abandoned. Most experts believe that Machu Picchu was built in the 1400s during the rule of the Inca emperor Pachacuti. The city was probably home to nobles, priests, and skilled workers rather than a large population. People grew crops on stone terraces that covered the mountainside. They also collected fresh water through a system of carefully planned canals and fountains. These features allowed people to live comfortably in a place that was difficult to reach. One of the most impressive features of Machu Picchu is its stonework. The Inca builders shaped huge stones so carefully that they fit together without mortar. This method made the buildings strong enough to survive many earthquakes. Even after hundreds of years of wind, rain, and earthquakes, much of the city still stands. Machu Picchu shows that the Inca people were not only skilled builders but also talented engineers who understood both nature and architecture.

