  ('english-word-152', 'english', 'choice', '단어 4 · 9월 학력평가', 'adequacy', 'inadequacy(부적절함)의 반대말로 필기한 adequacy의 뜻과 품사는?', null, '(명) 적절성', array['(형) 적절한', '(명) 목표(= objective)', '(명) 시각 예술가(화가, 조각가)'], '{}'::text[], 'adequacy: 명사 "적절성"의 뜻이다.', '영어 학습지4 · 2쪽 단어 필기', null, null, null, 321, null, null),
  ('english-word-153', 'english', 'choice', '단어 4 · 9월 학력평가', 'adequate', 'adequacy 아래에 필기한 adequate의 뜻과 품사는?', null, '(형) 적절한, 충분한', array['(명) 적절성', '(형) 보편적인', '(형) 동료의'], '{}'::text[], 'adequate: 형용사 "적절한, 충분한"의 뜻이다.', '영어 학습지4 · 2쪽 단어 필기', null, null, null, 322, null, null),
  ('english-written-001', 'english', 'written', '고대 건축물', null, '‘Made of carved stone, the temple still stands.’를 Because로 시작하는 부사절 문장으로 바꾸시오.', 'Chichén Itzá was a major city of the Maya Empire from A.D. 750 to 1200. Made of stepped pyramids, temples, and other stone structures, the ancient city is now one of Mexico’s most visited tourist destinations. The largest building in Chichén Itzá is the Temple of Kukulkan ―a pyramid with 365 steps. A kind of calendar, the temple shows the change of seasons. On the spring and autumn equinoxes each year, a shadow falls on the pyramid in the shape of a snake. As the sun sets, this shadowy snake goes down the steps to eventually join a carved snake head on the pyramid’s side. The Mayans constructed the pyramids with carved stone. Amazingly, they worked without wheels or metal tools. To build a pyramid, Mayan workers created a base and added smaller and smaller levels as the structure rose. Building the pyramids required many workers. Some pyramids took hundreds of years to complete. Chichén Itzá was both an advanced city center and a religious site. Spanish records show that the Mayans made human sacrifices to a rain god here. Archaeologists have found bones, jewelry, and other objects that people wore when they were sacrificed. Experts also know that the Mayans were knowledgeable astronomers. They used the tops of the pyramids to view Venus and other planets.

[연습용 문장·표현]
‘Made of carved stone, the temple still stands.’를 Because로 시작하는 부사절 문장으로 바꾸시오.', 'Because it is made of carved stone, the temple still stands.', '{}'::text[], array['Because + 주어 it + be동사 is 복원', 'made of carved stone 유지', '주절 the temple still stands 유지'], '', '학습지1', 1, null, null, 1000, null, null),
  ('english-written-002', 'english', 'written', '고대 건축물', null, '‘As the sun sets, the shadow goes down the steps.’를 분사구문으로 바꾸시오. 두 절의 주어가 다르다는 점에 주의하시오.', 'Chichén Itzá was a major city of the Maya Empire from A.D. 750 to 1200. Made of stepped pyramids, temples, and other stone structures, the ancient city is now one of Mexico’s most visited tourist destinations. The largest building in Chichén Itzá is the Temple of Kukulkan ―a pyramid with 365 steps. A kind of calendar, the temple shows the change of seasons. On the spring and autumn equinoxes each year, a shadow falls on the pyramid in the shape of a snake. As the sun sets, this shadowy snake goes down the steps to eventually join a carved snake head on the pyramid’s side. The Mayans constructed the pyramids with carved stone. Amazingly, they worked without wheels or metal tools. To build a pyramid, Mayan workers created a base and added smaller and smaller levels as the structure rose. Building the pyramids required many workers. Some pyramids took hundreds of years to complete. Chichén Itzá was both an advanced city center and a religious site. Spanish records show that the Mayans made human sacrifices to a rain god here. Archaeologists have found bones, jewelry, and other objects that people wore when they were sacrificed. Experts also know that the Mayans were knowledgeable astronomers. They used the tops of the pyramids to view Venus and other planets.

[연습용 문장·표현]
‘As the sun sets, the shadow goes down the steps.’를 분사구문으로 바꾸시오. 두 절의 주어가 다르다는 점에 주의하시오.', 'The sun setting, the shadow goes down the steps.', '{}'::text[], array['주어가 다르므로 The sun을 남김', 'sets → setting, 접속사 As 생략', '쉼표와 주절 유지'], '', '학습지1', 1, null, null, 1001, null, null),
  ('english-written-003', 'english', 'written', '고대 건축물', null, '‘그 구조물은 수십 개의 돌기둥으로 구성되어 있다.’를 consist of로 한 번, be composed of로 한 번 영작하시오.', 'Göbekli Tepe, in southeastern Türkiye, is one of the oldest man-made structures on Earth. Experts believe it was built about 12,000 years ago. The structure consists of dozens of stone pillars arranged in rings. Many pillars are covered with carvings of animals. The tallest pillars are 5.5 meters in height and weigh more than 14,500 kilograms. At the time that Göbekli Tepe was built, there was no writing system, and people did not use metal. Even wheels did not exist. Amazingly, though, the builders were able to cut, shape, and transport 16-ton stones. Archaeologists found Stone Age tools such as knives at the site. They think hundreds of workers carved and put the pillars in place. Archaeologists are still debating the purpose of Göbekli Tepe. Klaus Schmidt ― the archaeologist who originally excavated the site ― believed that Göbekli Tepe was a holy meeting place. According to his theory, the T-shaped pillars represent human beings. The pillars face the center of the circle and perhaps represent a religious ceremony. New evidence suggests that large feasts took place at the site. Archaeologists found thousands of small animal bones nearby, with stone containers large enough to hold more than 150 liters of liquid. They also found smaller pillars similar to Göbekli Tepe’s in areas over 200 kilometers away. It’s as though Göbekli Tepe were a cathedral and the other structures were local churches.

[연습용 문장·표현]
‘그 구조물은 수십 개의 돌기둥으로 구성되어 있다.’를 consist of로 한 번, be composed of로 한 번 영작하시오.', 'The structure consists of dozens of stone pillars. / The structure is composed of dozens of stone pillars.', '{}'::text[], array['consists of (3인칭 단수 현재, 수동태 아님)', 'is composed of', 'dozens of stone pillars'], '', '학습지1', 2, null, null, 1002, null, null),
  ('english-written-004', 'english', 'written', '고대 건축물', null, '‘At the time that Göbekli Tepe was built, there was no writing system.’에서 that을 다른 관계부사로 바꿔 쓰고, 바꿀 수 있는 이유를 쓰시오.', 'Göbekli Tepe, in southeastern Türkiye, is one of the oldest man-made structures on Earth. Experts believe it was built about 12,000 years ago. The structure consists of dozens of stone pillars arranged in rings. Many pillars are covered with carvings of animals. The tallest pillars are 5.5 meters in height and weigh more than 14,500 kilograms. At the time that Göbekli Tepe was built, there was no writing system, and people did not use metal. Even wheels did not exist. Amazingly, though, the builders were able to cut, shape, and transport 16-ton stones. Archaeologists found Stone Age tools such as knives at the site. They think hundreds of workers carved and put the pillars in place. Archaeologists are still debating the purpose of Göbekli Tepe. Klaus Schmidt ― the archaeologist who originally excavated the site ― believed that Göbekli Tepe was a holy meeting place. According to his theory, the T-shaped pillars represent human beings. The pillars face the center of the circle and perhaps represent a religious ceremony. New evidence suggests that large feasts took place at the site. Archaeologists found thousands of small animal bones nearby, with stone containers large enough to hold more than 150 liters of liquid. They also found smaller pillars similar to Göbekli Tepe’s in areas over 200 kilometers away. It’s as though Göbekli Tepe were a cathedral and the other structures were local churches.

[연습용 문장·표현]
‘At the time that Göbekli Tepe was built, there was no writing system.’에서 that을 다른 관계부사로 바꿔 쓰고, 바꿀 수 있는 이유를 쓰시오.', 'At the time when Göbekli Tepe was built, there was no writing system. 선행사 the time이 시간을 나타내므로 that 자리에 관계부사 when을 쓸 수 있다.', '{}'::text[], array['that → when', '선행사 the time(시간)', '나머지 문장 그대로 유지'], '', '학습지1', 2, null, null, 1003, null, null),
  ('english-written-005', 'english', 'written', '공통 문법', null, '두 문장의 though를 비교하시오. (a) It’s as though it were a cathedral. (b) Amazingly, though, they moved the stones. 각각의 뜻과 품사를 쓰시오.', 'Göbekli Tepe, in southeastern Türkiye, is one of the oldest man-made structures on Earth. Experts believe it was built about 12,000 years ago. The structure consists of dozens of stone pillars arranged in rings. Many pillars are covered with carvings of animals. The tallest pillars are 5.5 meters in height and weigh more than 14,500 kilograms. At the time that Göbekli Tepe was built, there was no writing system, and people did not use metal. Even wheels did not exist. Amazingly, though, the builders were able to cut, shape, and transport 16-ton stones. Archaeologists found Stone Age tools such as knives at the site. They think hundreds of workers carved and put the pillars in place. Archaeologists are still debating the purpose of Göbekli Tepe. Klaus Schmidt ― the archaeologist who originally excavated the site ― believed that Göbekli Tepe was a holy meeting place. According to his theory, the T-shaped pillars represent human beings. The pillars face the center of the circle and perhaps represent a religious ceremony. New evidence suggests that large feasts took place at the site. Archaeologists found thousands of small animal bones nearby, with stone containers large enough to hold more than 150 liters of liquid. They also found smaller pillars similar to Göbekli Tepe’s in areas over 200 kilometers away. It’s as though Göbekli Tepe were a cathedral and the other structures were local churches.

[연습용 문장·표현]
두 문장의 though를 비교하시오. (a) It’s as though it were a cathedral. (b) Amazingly, though, they moved the stones. 각각의 뜻과 품사를 쓰시오.', '(a)의 as though는 as if와 같은 접속사로 "마치 ~인 것처럼"이며 뒤에 가정법 과거 were가 왔다. (b)의 though는 콤마 사이에 홀로 쓰인 부사로 "그러나"(=however)이다.', '{}'::text[], array['(a) as though = as if, 마치 ~인 것처럼', '(a) 가정법 과거 were', '(b) 부사, 그러나 = however'], '', '학습지1', 2, null, null, 1004, null, null),
  ('english-written-006', 'english', 'written', '공통 문법', null, 'allow와 make를 각각 사용해 ‘그 도구는 그들이 돌을 옮기게 했다.’를 과거시제로 두 문장 쓰시오.', 'For hundreds of years, Machu Picchu remained hidden in the Andes Mountains of Peru. In 1911, an American explorer named Hiram Bingham introduced the ancient city to the world after local people guided him there. Today, millions of visitors travel to see its beautiful stone buildings and breathtaking mountain views. Although many facts about Machu Picchu are known, historians still debate why the city was built and why it was later abandoned. Most experts believe that Machu Picchu was built in the 1400s during the rule of the Inca emperor Pachacuti. The city was probably home to nobles, priests, and skilled workers rather than a large population. People grew crops on stone terraces that covered the mountainside. They also collected fresh water through a system of carefully planned canals and fountains. These features allowed people to live comfortably in a place that was difficult to reach. One of the most impressive features of Machu Picchu is its stonework. The Inca builders shaped huge stones so carefully that they fit together without mortar. This method made the buildings strong enough to survive many earthquakes. Even after hundreds of years of wind, rain, and earthquakes, much of the city still stands. Machu Picchu shows that the Inca people were not only skilled builders but also talented engineers who understood both nature and architecture.

[연습용 문장·표현]
allow와 make를 각각 사용해 ‘그 도구는 그들이 돌을 옮기게 했다.’를 과거시제로 두 문장 쓰시오.', 'The tool allowed them to move the stones. / The tool made them move the stones.', '{}'::text[], array['allowed + them + to move', 'made + them + move(동사원형)', '과거시제와 the stones'], '', '학습지1', 3, null, null, 1005, null, null),
  ('english-written-007', 'english', 'written', '고대 건축물', null, '‘이 방법은 건물들을 지진을 견딜 만큼 충분히 튼튼하게 만들었다.’를 enough to를 사용해 영작하시오.', 'For hundreds of years, Machu Picchu remained hidden in the Andes Mountains of Peru. In 1911, an American explorer named Hiram Bingham introduced the ancient city to the world after local people guided him there. Today, millions of visitors travel to see its beautiful stone buildings and breathtaking mountain views. Although many facts about Machu Picchu are known, historians still debate why the city was built and why it was later abandoned. Most experts believe that Machu Picchu was built in the 1400s during the rule of the Inca emperor Pachacuti. The city was probably home to nobles, priests, and skilled workers rather than a large population. People grew crops on stone terraces that covered the mountainside. They also collected fresh water through a system of carefully planned canals and fountains. These features allowed people to live comfortably in a place that was difficult to reach. One of the most impressive features of Machu Picchu is its stonework. The Inca builders shaped huge stones so carefully that they fit together without mortar. This method made the buildings strong enough to survive many earthquakes. Even after hundreds of years of wind, rain, and earthquakes, much of the city still stands. Machu Picchu shows that the Inca people were not only skilled builders but also talented engineers who understood both nature and architecture.

